# `tauri dev` file-watcher filter (gitignore syntax, relative to this file).
#
# The Tauri CLI watches `src-tauri/` and every workspace crate it depends on,
# and kills, rebuilds and relaunches the desktop app on any event that survives
# this filter. `.gitignore` does NOT filter events below a watched folder, so a
# generated or staged file inside one restarts the app (the window reopens at
# `/` with all state lost, which reads as "HMR is broken"). List here only
# outputs whose change never needs a native rebuild.

# Staged by predev/prebuild scripts (stage-bundled-plugins, prepare-plugin-node,
# stage-browser-runtime); read from disk at runtime, never compiled in.
src-tauri/resources/plugins/
src-tauri/resources/plugin-node/
src-tauri/resources/browser-runtime/

# Release sidecars written by `pnpm tauri build`'s beforeBuildCommand.
src-tauri/binaries/

# Written by build.rs / tauri-build during the build the watcher just started:
# `all-app-commands.toml` is derived from `src/lib.rs` (which is watched), and
# `gen/` holds the generated ACL schemas.
src-tauri/permissions/all-app-commands.toml
src-tauri/gen/

# Interpreter and editor droppings anywhere under a watched crate.
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.swp
*.swo
*~
